---
name: "Fix Tests"
description: "Fixes build, typecheck, and test failures from the verify check"
tags: [build, verify]
stage: build
---

<artifact id="fix-tests">

<task>
The verify check (build & full test suite) failed.
Read the check output to identify every failure.
Fix each failure at its root cause — prefer correcting code or tests over weakening assertions.
Re-run the same verification commands to confirm all suites pass before finishing.
</task>

<dependencies>
Read the context files before fixing:
- `${{ openspecChangeDir }}/proposal.md`
- `${{ openspecChangeDir }}/design.md`
- `${{ openspecChangeDir }}/tasks.json`
- relevant specs under `${{ openspecChangeDir }}/specs/`
- `${{ openspecChangeDir }}/progress.txt` if it exists — prior tasks' recorded
  decisions, gotchas, and established patterns. Read the `## Codebase Patterns`
  section first.
</dependencies>

<instruction>
1. Read the check output to see the exact failures.
2. Understand what the build stage was implementing by reading proposal.md, design.md, tasks.json, and specs.
3. Fix each failure at its root cause:
   - For build/compilation errors: fix the code.
   - For typecheck errors: fix the types.
   - For test failures: fix the code or tests — do not weaken assertions unless the original assertion was wrong.
4. After fixing, re-run the failed verification plus the test and typecheck
   suites that cover the changed area.
5. Confirm they pass before marking the task complete.
</instruction>

<repair_policy>
- Do not weaken assertions or remove tests to make them pass.
- Do not make unrelated changes.
- Stay within the scope of the current change as described in proposal.md and tasks.json.
- You may be interrupted at any time: commit incrementally and keep your progress
  notes current.
</repair_policy>

<progress_tracking>
`${{ openspecChangeDir }}/progress.txt` is this issue's working memory.
Record noteworthy discoveries as you work — patterns, decisions, gotchas,
anything that might help later steps. Don't think about structure — just append.
Before finishing, review and make sure your key learnings are recorded.
</progress_tracking>

<completion>
When you have completed all work for this task, output `<promise>done</promise>`
at the end of your response. If you have NOT completed the task, output
`<promise>unfinished</promise>` instead.
</completion>

</artifact>
